+# BoardSession Code - OSS integration snapshot
+
+A local reconstruction of the described internal integration, **not a copy of the company tree or its exact diff**.
+
+- `board-session/`: full `@carizon/board-session` npm source, compiled `dist`, native addon, wolfSSH/wolfSSL shared objects and public headers under `build/wolfssh` and `build/wolfssl`.
+- `src/extension.ts`: an extension activation API that returns the npm package exports (`BoardSession`), without adding any commands, menus, or user interaction. Access from another extension using `vscode.extensions.getExtension('carizon.boardsession')?.activate()`.
+- `board-session/debug/client-identity.pem`: internal debug composite identity copied from `remotessh`; **ignored by Git but intentionally included in this local snapshot's npm/VSIX packaging** as the requested default. Never distribute these artifacts externally.
+- `esbuild.mts`: deliberately externalizes the nested npm import to preserve worker/native module relative paths.
+
+VS Code's `build/gulpfile.extensions.ts` includes the extension's tsconfig in the standard extension compilation list; `build/npm/dirs.ts` installs both the extension's and npm package's dependencies; `build/lib/extensions.ts` classifies `boardsession` as native and explicitly includes the `ssh2` runtime dependency tree in desktop packaging. It is not enabled for web builds or registered in user interaction flows.
+
+Build just the npm package: `npm --prefix extensions/boardsession/board-session run build` (libraries and headers are already staged). Produce an npm tarball: `cd extensions/boardsession/board-session && npm pack`. The root extension's `compile` uses `extensions/esbuild-extension-common.mts` and expects the VS Code root toolchain to have been installed; do **not** run a full Code - OSS build for this snapshot.
+
+The shared objects currently target **Linux x64 only** (`prebuilds/linux-x64`). This local reconstruction does not establish Windows support for the company's VS Code build: a Windows host requires Windows native artifacts and corresponding wolf libraries. The extension API does not implement editor UI integration.
+
+Source baselines: Code - OSS `bc66acbf`, BoardSession `f508c1a`, wolf `77105bf`.
+
+## Chat terminal routing
+
+The Copilot Chat view title has a plug button that prompts for a board and zero or more password-authenticated jump servers. After connecting it enables `board_terminal_run/send/output/kill` and hides the corresponding built-in terminal tools (plus the local `execution_subagent`) from tool discovery. Clicking the disconnect icon closes the remote session and restores local terminal tools. No Copilot extension sources are patched.
+
+The debug X.509 private key is bundled **only because this local internal snapshot explicitly requests it as the default**. It is a shared credential, not a secure production provisioning mechanism: restrict distribution of any npm/VSIX artifacts containing it and replace it with per-user provisioning before sharing the extension. `debug/client-identity.pem` stays ignored by git, so the local file needs to be present when building a package.
